nodecode-fivedive is a rewrite of 5dive-ai's 5dive-ai/5dive-plugins:

  https://github.com/5dive-ai/5dive-plugins
  commit d9e8ad1ad0f6e109d54a213e743d25284389f875
  Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC (LICENSE), the repository's own
  NOTICE naming 5dive as the holder of the plugins (NOTICE)

The rewritten plugin is the folder plugins/dashboard/hermes of that commit
(plugin.yaml, __init__.py, adapter.py, README.md). What was carried over: the
spool protocol in both directions, one JSON file per message in inbox/ and one
per reply in outbox/<chat>/, with the temp-name-then-rename write on both
sides; the message shape (text, route.source of dashboard, route.chat_id,
route.voice, image_path, received_at); the rule that an inbox file is removed
before its message is handed on and a file that is not a valid message is
dropped rather than left to trip every lap; the admission setting, the
5dive-app sender the bridge writes as and the single-owner trust argument that
comes with the folder; the 16000-character message cap; the reply word cap,
with the same count outside fenced code, the same refusal, the same two
rewrites and the same fall-through to the long answer as written; the voice
note answered by voice, marked on the next reply; the upload path named in a
message; the standalone sender the original registers for out-of-process use,
here the fivedive_send tool and /fivedive; and the platform hint the original
gives the model in words, shaped to the prompt this cell submits.

What was left out, and why: the Hermes gateway plumbing itself - the platform
registration, the adapter class, the asyncio poll loop, connect/disconnect
and the SendResult shapes - because a cell submits through NLE:SUBMIT and the
session's own answer instead; the profile-scoped secret reader, since a cell's
section is already per-home; FIVEDIVE_HOME_CHANNEL and cron delivery, since a
scheduled turn can reach the chat through fivedive_send; and the 5dive bridge
(plugins/dashboard/server.ts) and everything on the 5dive side of the spool,
which this cell does not replace and does not need to know about. An upload is
named in the prompt rather than attached as an image, because the spool hands
over a path on this box and the agent can read it with its own tools.
LICENSE is the repository's LICENSE, unchanged.
